---
// Goal: show how ThinkThen asks a decision model that Ollama serves on your own machine, with no key and no hosted service.
import SidePage from '../../../layouts/SidePage.astro';
import Terminal from '../../../components/Terminal.astro';
import BackendFacts from '../../../components/BackendFacts.astro';
import { BACKEND_PAGES, BACKENDS_SEE } from '../../../data/catalog.mjs';
import { captioned } from '../../../data/samples.mjs';
import { backend } from '../../../lib/backends-table.mjs';
import { checkLines } from '../../../data/backend-checks.mjs';
import CheckLines from '../../../components/CheckLines.astro';

const page = BACKEND_PAGES.find((p) => p.slug === 'ollama');
const b = backend('ollama');
const runs = captioned('install/backends/ollama', BACKENDS_SEE.ollama);
const by = (name) => runs.find((r) => r.name.endsWith(name));
const [plan, one, lines, tev1] = ['check-plan', 'one', 'lines', 'tev1'].map(by);
const checks = checkLines('ollama');
---
<SidePage pages={BACKEND_PAGES} page={{ ...page, description: 'Ollama serves decision models such as nimble and tev1 on your own machine. ThinkThen asks them with --backend ollama.' }} name="Backends">
  <h1>Ollama</h1>
  <p class="lede">Ollama 0.35 and later serve System One on your own machine. ThinkThen asks them with <code>--backend {b.name}</code>, with no key and no hosted service.</p>

  <BackendFacts name="ollama" notes={{ key: 'not needed on this machine', model: 'Name <code>tev1</code> with <code>--model tev1</code>.' }} />

  <h2>Set it up</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Install Ollama 0.35 or later from <a href="https://ollama.com/download">ollama.com</a>.</li>
    <li>Run <code>ollama pull {b.model}</code>, and <code>ollama pull tev1</code> for the smaller model.</li>
    <li>Ask with <code>--backend {b.name}</code>. On this machine ThinkThen sends no key.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>The examples below run Ollama on a second port, 11535, beside another Ollama on the same machine. So each one names the port with <code>--url</code>. On the default port, leave it out. A local Ollama needs no key at any port.</p>

  <h2>Descriptions travel as text</h2>
  <p>Ollama refuses a description written as an object. So this backend alone sends each description as its text. An object's <code>what</code> goes, and its other fields stay behind. The plan says so on its first line.</p>
  <Terminal run={plan} caption={plan.see} />
  {checks.length
    ? <Fragment><CheckLines name="ollama" /><p>Each warning names a description sent as text. Ollama 0.35 ran on the second port for these checks.</p></Fragment>
    : <p>No live check against Ollama is on record for this page.</p>}

  {one && lines ? (
    <Fragment>
      <h2>Ask nimble</h2>
      <Terminal run={one} caption={one.see} />
      <Terminal run={lines} caption={lines.see} />
    </Fragment>
  ) : (
    <p>This page shows no recorded Ollama answer. The <a href="/install/backends/typesafe/">TypeSafe Jev page</a> asks the same two questions.</p>
  )}
  {tev1 && (
    <Fragment>
      <h2>Ask tev1</h2>
      <Terminal run={tev1} caption={tev1.see} />
    </Fragment>
  )}

  <p>A pulled model can change under the same name. After a new pull, pass <code>--refresh-cache</code> once. It asks every question again and replaces the answers in the answer cache.</p>

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/install/backends/">All backends</a> · <a href="/install/configuration/">Configuration</a></p>
</SidePage>
